/-!
# Exact cyclic Fourier coefficient data for the J₁ rows

`coefficients j i` gives the integer multiplicities of the powers of a linear
character for row `i` on a class-`j` generator. `quotients` certifies equality
with the literal power table modulo the cyclotomic polynomial `modulus j`.
The soundness proofs and every finite check are in `Fourier.lean`.

The table and derived numerical data retain the GPL-3.0-or-later attribution
to Thomas Breuer's GAP CTblLib 1.3.11, entry J1, documented in the ancestor
`ModularCharacters/Source.md` and its `GPL-3.0.txt`. No GAP or Python output is
trusted as a proof. The accompanying generator uses exact integer arithmetic.
Source: Janko (1966), ordinary-character calculation; Gorenstein §16.6, p.482.
-/

